| `agents.max_model_calls` | integer | `0` | a whole number, 0 or more | `models/budget.py` (`approved_cap`); `scripts/model_budget.py` (`cap`, `approve`); `scripts/doc_review.py`; `scripts/refactor_practice.py`; `scripts/hooks/on_stop_doc_review.py`; `scripts/hooks/on_stop_triage.py`; `mcp/qa_server.py` (`configured_cap`) | The approved cap on the model calls one agent `--execute` run may make: a run whose bound (`--max-chunks`, `--max-nodes`, or one call for triage) is over it, or negative so it bounds nothing, is refused with exit 2 before any model is built, and `0` approves none. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] agents.max_model_calls = 0` to stderr; a value that is not a whole number of 0 or more is refused with exit 14. The run is then held to its bound as a count of the calls made: each call goes through a `models.CountedModel`, and the call past the bound stops the run with exit 1 naming the count. A saved run under `wiki/.runtime/` resumes only on the model the run names and with no more calls left than its bound, or is refused with exit 2 naming the snapshot to remove. `mcp/qa_server.py` reads it once at start and holds each question to it: `0` answers every question with a tool error naming this key. The count is per question; the server's total over its lifetime is `agents.max_session_model_calls`. A dry run is never held to it. | the eval harness's live cap: `evals.live.max_calls` | always |
